  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Glyptothorax cavia (Hamilton, 1822)</li><li>Common name: Heart Throat Catfish</li><li>Type locality: Patgong, northern Bengal, India.</li><li>Sexing: not known.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>Asia: Pakistan, India, Nepal, Bangladesh, Myanmar and China.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>Sisorid catfishes of the genus Glyptothorax are benthic inhabitants of torrential waters of rivers and streams in montane and submontane parts of tropical Asia. They attach themselves to rocks and boulders against strong currents by means of a thoracic adhesive apparatus comprising grooves and folded pleats of skin.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>The water should be cool and heavily oxygenated with a good flow, as these fish occur in hill streams. Anything above 25 °C will hamper long-term survival, as these fish tend to burn away at higher temperatures.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>Fine sand for the bottom and smooth pebbles / rocks.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>Is known to take only live food like bloodworms, frozen brine shrimp etc. Spot feeding will help in case tank mates are voracious feeders.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>A peaceful species suitable for a hillstream biotope. Suggested tankmates: cyprinids like Barilius and Danios, and balitorine loaches like Homaloptera species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>Unreported in the aquarium. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1446",
      "html": "<p>An account of the fishes found in the river Ganges, pp 188, 378.</p>"
    }
  ],
